de3 on a private 10.50.50.0/24 network reachable via their second NIC (eth1 on node1, ens7 on node2/node3). Added VyOS source NAT masquerade rule 100 (source 10.50.50.0/24 -> outbound eth0) and committed/saved config. On node2/node3, statically configured ens7 (10.50.50.11/.12) and added a low-metric (50) default route via node1 (10.50.50.254) on ens7, so ordinary process traffic egresses through node1's NAT while their pre-existing management-network route remains as a fallback. Verified NAT translation via conntrack on node1 (src 10.50.50.11/.12 translated to node1's WAN IP 10.100.62.10) and confirmed internet reachability (ping/curl) from both node2 and node3 sourced on ens7. Completed the mandatory restart protocol: captured pre-restart boot_id baselines on all three nodes, restarted node1, node2, and node3 sequentially (one at a time) via native `reboot`, confirmed each node's boot_id changed after reconnecting, and verified post-restart that NAT config persisted on node1 (VyOS `show nat` still shows rule 100) and that node2/node3 retained their static IP/route config and successfully reached the internet through node1 again.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected topology and interfaces on node1/node2/node3 (dual-NIC each: management network 10.100.62.0/24, unaddressed private network via eth1/ens7)\",\"Configured node1 eth1 = 10.50.50.254/24 and VyOS NAT source rule 100 (10.50.50.0/24 -> masquerade via eth0), committed and saved\",\"Configured node2 ens7 = 10.50.50.11/24 with persistent /etc/network/interfaces.d/ens7.cfg and added default route via 10.50.50.254 metric 50\",\"Configured node3 ens7 = 10.50.50.12/24 with persistent /etc/network/interfaces.d/ens7.cfg and added default route via 10.50.50.254 metric 50\",\"Verified NAT translation via conntrack on node1 and successful ping/curl to the internet from node2 and node3 over ens7\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id baseline on all three nodes\",\"Restarted node1 via native reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, verified NAT config persisted and node2/node3 connectivity restored\",\"Restarted node2 via native reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, verified static IP/route persisted and internet reachable via node1\",\"Restarted node3 via native reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, verified static IP/route persisted and internet reachable via node1\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node1 provides NAT so node2/node3 processes reach the internet\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-20b3c325286444b7\",\"cmd-8be05c0c50d346bd\",\"cmd-2896032ccd2c43a0\",\"cmd-1946eefe7b5849af\",\"cmd-da16a1ff85fa4956\"],\"summary\":\"VyOS NAT source rule 100 (10.50.50.0/24 -> masquerade via eth0) committed on node1; ping/curl succeed from node2 and node3 over the private ens7 interface; conntrack on node1 shows live translation of 10.50.50.11/.12 traffic to node1's WAN IP 10.100.62.10\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 healthy baseline and restart evidence\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2da7ae2fdefb4e77\",\"cmd-6f13902459ac4047\",\"cmd-1062ab611b8949a7\",\"cmd-5a83f73446904300\",\"cmd-851883a5dede4d1c\",\"cmd-e9f868eddb6f4527\",\"cmd-0825f64b60264096\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id e98d9010... captured; reboot acknowledged and returned before disconnect; connection dropped confirming reboot in progress; reconnected with new boot_id c25c37e2...; post-restart config (eth1 address, NAT rule 100) confirmed intact\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 healthy baseline and restart evidence\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a7029405ae584d80\",\"cmd-f90c5a44c2d0457e\",\"cmd-bef18cb14a3942ce\",\"cmd-a18d0a0a08b04587\",\"cmd-32e8f6bd5a11463c\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id f6f9440e... captured; reboot acknowledged, SSH connection refused confirming reboot; reconnected with new boot_id 1ca610a9...; post-restart static IP/route config intact and internet reachable via node1\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 healthy baseline and restart evidence\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3aa323f6631144e0\",